WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.859
A core alone cannot boot a complete Linux system.

2
00:00:03.859 --> 00:00:11.498
It needs a suitable configuration, memory, interrupts, peripherals and a matching software stack.

3
00:00:11.498 --> 00:00:17.168
The CVA6 repository contains an application processing unit environment.

4
00:00:17.168 --> 00:00:21.814
The separate CVA6 SDK provides a board-oriented Linux flow.

5
00:00:21.814 --> 00:00:27.485
Cheshire is another host platform built around CVA6 in the PULP project.

6
00:00:27.485 --> 00:00:30.713
These are related but distinct artifacts.

7
00:00:30.713 --> 00:00:39.140
Choose a documented platform and its software together; enabling an MMU is not a complete integration plan.

